{"parentUuid":"5f09162d-75d5-4cc0-8d4a-e664df72e53c","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/workspace/repo","sessionId":"0eff23df-da0c-4fcc-830e-33d0fd9a9e39","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"feature/01_homepage-and-learn-page-20260319-155250","agentId":"adafd0ba72022e48e","slug":"dapper-wishing-volcano","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0187nWYSgnebqJ1jPwoVVrme","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Design: Homepage and Learn Page
     2→
     3→## Overview
     4→New Angular v21 project with Taiga UI, two routes (home and learn), SCSS theming inspired by bunny.net, and Playwright tests as a visual demo.
     5→
     6→## Key Decisions
     7→
     8→### Taiga UI as component library
     9→**Choice:** Taiga UI for all UI components
    10→**Rationale:** Explicitly chosen by the user. Provides Angular-native components, good theming support for light/dark mode, and a professional look.
    11→
    12→### Bunny.net-inspired color palette
    13→**Choice:** Blue-based palette with orange accents (`#183d6d`, `#052740` for blue; `#fd8d32` → `#ffaf48` for orange)
    14→**Rationale:** The bunny.net style — clean, modern, premium appearance — fits well for a tool that aims to be free and professional.
    15→
    16→### Playwright as e2e and visual demo
    17→**Choice:** Playwright tests run via `npx playwright test --ui` on the VPS. VSCode Remote SSH automatically forwards the port so the Playwright UI can be opened in the local browser. Tests can be followed live step-by-step with screenshots.
    18→**Rationale:** Dual purpose — tests validate page content, and UI mode serves as a live demo. No extra software needed (no VNC/Xvfb), works out-of-the-box with VSCode port forwarding.
    19→
    20→### Multi-language support from day 1
    21→**Choice:** Angular built-in i18n (compile-time per locale) with NL, DE, EN
    22→**Rationale:** Adding i18n after the fact is a lot of work. Angular built-in i18n generates an optimized bundle per language. By setting it up immediately, future features only need to add translations.
    23→
    24→## Components Affected
    25→- **AppComponent** — root component with header navigation and theme toggle
    26→- **HomeComponent** — hero section, feature highlights, call-to-action
    27→- **LearnComponent** — placeholder page with structure for future training exercises
    28→- **AppRoutingModule** — routes for `/` (home) and `/learn`
    29→- **Theme** — SCSS variables and Taiga UI theme configuration for light/dark
    30→
    31→## Data Model Changes
    32→None — pure frontend, no data storage.
    33→
    34→## API Changes
    35→None — no backend.
    36→
    37→## Risks and Mitigations
    38→| Risk | Likelihood | Mitigation |
    39→|------|-----------|------------|
    40→| Taiga UI compatibility with Angular v21 | Medium | Check compatibility beforehand; fall back to standalone components if needed |
    41→| Angular i18n compile-time complexity | Low | Configure locales early; use `ng extract-i18n` for translation files |
    42→| Bunny.net style difficult to replicate | Low | Focus on color palette and spacing, not a pixel-perfect copy |
    43→"}]},"uuid":"cf92fa55-be1e-4334-9205-35ded0e57e08","timestamp":"2026-03-19T16:22:05.968Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5f09162d-75d5-4cc0-8d4a-e664df72e53c"}
